1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,900
This is Raelyn, your private semantic observatory.
It keeps unfolding events from getting lost in the stream.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,800
It extracts facts from video and gathers related events
into a starfield you can replay and explore.

3
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:15,200
Events cluster by meaning, giving information structure.

4
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:18,600
Drill into any cluster and return to its sources and evidence.

5
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:22,100
Evidence-backed links connect these events into stories.

6
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:25,300
Stories evolve across snapshots, always tied to evidence.

7
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:29,300
Choose a time span. Observation briefs turn it
into a complete, citable narrative.

8
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:33,700
Explanations lead back to video, transcripts, and context.

9
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,000
Every source under continuous watch flows into one library.

10
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:40,400
Material becomes searchable, traceable long-term memory.

11
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:44,600
Work from collection to analysis stays fully observable.

12
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:47,600
Calls, model usage, downloads, and storage share one ledger.

13
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:50,300
Long-term observation costs stay clear and controlled.

14
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:53,700
Through MCP, agents enter the same semantic world.

15
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:57,200
Explore Raelyn on GitHub
https://github.com/scisaga/raelyn
